{%- set thing = feature.thing -%}
<li class="feature h-entry"{% if thing.story %} style="--cover: {{ thing.story.color }}"{% endif %}>
  {#- The cover is the front page the collector last captured, linked like the thing page's screenshot; a thing
      with no capture (a repository, say) shows its sticker on its story colour. The visit link says the same
      thing in words, so the cover is hidden from the keyboard and screen readers. Both links carry
      ?ref=xyz-featured where Tinylytics counts the site (feature.href and feature.cover, collection/site.ts). #}
  {#- An h-entry of the featured h-feed: the title links the thing's page (p-name, u-url). The card shows no
      date, so dt-published is an empty <data>, the thing page's date (started, else ended); it sits in the
      h3 because on a phone the card is a grid, where another child would take a cell. #}
  <a class="feature-cover" href="{{ feature.cover }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- if thing.screenshot %}<img src="{{ thing.screenshot.src }}" width="{{ thing.screenshot.width }}" height="{{ thing.screenshot.height }}" alt="" decoding="async" />
    {%- else %}<span class="feature-mark">{{ thing.sticker.letters }}</span>{% endif -%}
  </a>
  <h3><a class="p-name u-url" href="{{ thing.page }}">{{ thing.title }}</a>{% if thing.started or thing.ended %}<data class="dt-published" value="{{ thing.started or thing.ended }}"></data>{% endif %}</h3>
  <p class="feature-summary p-summary">{{ thing.summary }}</p>
  {% if feature.href %}<a class="feature-visit" href="{{ feature.href }}">{{ thing.url | displayUrl }}<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a>{% endif %}
</li>
